"logp":[{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"VO","value":0.27,"value_relation":"=","type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"water","doi":"10.1002/asia.70388","year":2025,"record_id":"MLDB-004319","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"Octanol-saturated water and water-saturated octanol were obtained by centrifuging deionised water for five minutes after stirring it with octanol for twenty-four hours. Prior to being combined with water-saturated octanol in volumetric ratios of 1:1, 1:2, and 2:1 in duplicate, the complex VO and nanoconjugate VO@AuNPs were dissolved in octanol-saturated water to a typical concentration of 0.03 to 3 mM and 0.03 to 3 mg/mL respectively. After 0.5 h of vortexing, the mixtures were centrifuged for 5 minutes. A fine gauge needle was used to separate the layers properly, and UV-visible spectroscopy was used to determine the nanoconjugate composition. The ratio of the nanoconjugate concentration in the octanol layer to that in the aqueous layer (P = coct/cwater) was used to calculate the partition coefficient."}]}